.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-harden
command performs some common system-hardening configurations
to help secure an OS installation.  The added security configurations
are by no means complete or appropriate for every system.  They
are simply a starting point from which system security can be
better tuned to specific needs.

This script is meant to be run as a first step following installation
of a security-sensitive system, to quickly improve security over the
default install while additional steps are taken to fully secure
the system.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

